<title>SINGAPORE: Aztech launches 56-speed modem.</title>
<headline>Aztech launches 56-speed modem.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-07-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Singapore's multimedia firm Aztech Systems said on Thursday it was launching a high speed 56K internal modem for the retail market.</p>
<p>Using just a standard analog telephone line, the modem, based on K56flex technology, allows transmission from Internet Service Providers Internet users at speeds of up to 56 kilobits per second.</p>
<p>The modem has a hardware-based architecture and so allows the central processing unit's power to be maximised for games, video conferencing, Internet phone and other applications.</p>
<p>The modem will be sold from August.  </p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom (65-8703080)</p>
